      <common:generalComment>Dataset developed according to Arcadia project Methodology (Report: “Metodologia per gli studi di filiera della Banca Dati italiana LCA”). LCA study of Cement production (report: “STUDIO LCA DELLA FILIERA DEL CEMENTO”).The dataset refers to the national average cement representative of the main types of cement defined by the UNI EN 197-1 produced in Italy, in particular: Portland cement (CEM I) and blended Portland cement (CEM II) (with total of 86%), pozzolanic cements (12%) and blast furnace cement (2%.). Data have been provided by AITEC/Federbeton and collected for the development of the EPD (Environmental Product Declaration) of the Italian medium gray cement. </common:generalComment>
      <referenceToExternalDocumentation type="source data set" refObjectId="a2b7ce21-8c82-45c1-84c9-d03086ed6139" version="01.00.000" uri="../sources/a2b7ce21-8c82-45c1-84c9-d03086ed6139.xml">
        <common:shortDescription>Sposato P., Luciano A., Corrado S., Altamura P., Rinaldi C., 2023. “STUDIO LCA DELLA FILIERA DEL CEMENTO”. Internal report ARCADIA Project. &#13;
Background datasets from Ecoinvent database cut-off (v.3.7.1) were used for the LCA study&#13;
</common:shortDescription>
      </referenceToExternalDocumentation>
    </dataSetInformation>
