    <technology>
      <technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>1t of average cement produced in Italy.&#13;
The cement production process includes the clinker and cement production stages. Clinker is produced from natural raw materials (such as limestone, clay, gypsum, marl and others) which are crushed, finely ground, homogenised and fired in a blast furnace. Once out, the clinker is cooled and ground in the mills with the addition of other natural raw materials (mainly gypsum and limestone) and other materials/additives to obtain the final homogeneous powder (the cement). &#13;
All the processes of the clinker and cement production stages, including transports and emissions to air, are foreground processes, modelled using primary data. &#13;
&#13;
Particularly:&#13;
•	Average data provided by the Italian Cement Techno-Economic Association (AITEC) for the years 2019 and 2020, representing 16.4% and 17% of national production respectively. Data provided by AITEC/Federbeton have been collected for the development of the EPD (Environmental Product Declaration) of the italian medium gray cement. &#13;
•	National average emission factors for the year 2019 (ISPRA, 2019) relating to clinker production (blast furnace process).&#13;
•	The study by Rigamonti et al. (2012) for modeling secondary solid fuel (SSF) production&#13;
•	Water consumption is modelled using primary data provided by a company part of the working group&#13;
For the background processes (raw material in input) EcoInvent database (v. 3.7.1) cut-off datasets were used. &#13;
&#13;
</technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>
      <technologicalApplicability>Production of italian average cement for construction sector</technologicalApplicability>
